\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} implemented. This is the list of the machine's switches in full, with the default configuration, its gates and its measurements, moved into the journal on 2026-11-24 with its wording unchanged. It is the state of the evening of 2026-11-24: the machine is the default engine, with the default switch set of wave 6 plus \code{eager}, \code{skipargs} and \code{congruence}. The times in it are UTC, and the date 2026-11-25 in its text is the UTC date of that evening. The short note [staging switches and the default switch set](design-switches) was written from an earlier state of the list (the set of wave 6, the machine not yet the default engine again); where the two differ, this document is the later state.}

\blockquote{
\p{\strong{STATE, 2026-11-25: THE MACHINE IS THE DEFAULT ENGINE} (\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} = 100) with the default switch set of 2026-11-25 (the set of wave 6 + \code{\verb~|eager,skipargs,congruence~}), under the owner's "practical" policy (\src{docs/design/OWNER-NOTES.md} note 13): never a statement that is not derivable; the official verdict on every real input; everything the official checker accepts is accepted (the reference engine re-checks every rejection and decides every decline); kind T accepts are tolerated and documented (\src{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md}). A run that means the reference engine says \code{\verb~|-X engine=reference~} or \code{\verb~|-X policy=strict~}. History: the machine was the default engine from 2026-11-24T19:41Z to 20:35Z (integration of wave 6) and was taken back because of the wrong accepts E1-F1 .. E1-F5 against the official checker; E1-F1 .. F6 are fixed (\code{\verb~|NOTES-M5.md~}), the remaining classes are kind T. Evidence for the switch back: the adversarial pass of reviewer S3 on exactly this set (no kind F; \src{docs/design/review/soundness-default-set.md} section 10), the hostile suite with kinds (1,196 rows; \code{\verb~|NOTES-S.md~}), the gates of the section "The default set of 2026-11-25", and the steward's gate on a machine-default distribution (\code{\verb~|scripts/gate.sh --defaults --corpus all --hostile~}: 230 / 230; 17,775 mutants SOUNDNESS 0 / COMPLETENESS 0; hostile 1,196 rows: 0 wrong accept, 0 wrong reject).}
}

\p{Every optimisation of the machine that changes what is computed sits behind a staging switch (\code{\verb~|Op.SW_*~}, \code{\verb~|Machine.sw~}, \code{\verb~|m.on(Op.SW_X)~}); a strict engine (\code{\verb~|EngineConfig.strict~}, the driver's re-check engine) runs with none, whatever is configured. This file is the single list: name, bit, owner, state, the gate and the measurement that justify the state. Owner of the file: M6 until 2026-11-24 17:19Z, then the integrator of wave 6 (\code{\verb~|work/status/machine-integration.md~}, heading "Wave 6": every run named here, with its command and its report file).}

\subtree{
\title{How switches are set}

\table{
\tr{\th{Where}\th{Form}}
\tr{\td{launcher}\td{\code{\verb~|-X machine.switches=LIST~} (or the system property \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.switches=LIST~}; \code{\verb~|-X~} wins)}}
\tr{\td{tests}\td{\code{\verb~|Fixture.switches("LIST")~}, \code{\verb~|Debug.parseSwitches("LIST")~}}}
\tr{\td{in code}\td{\code{\verb~|m.on(Op.SW_X)~}}}
}

\p{\code{\verb~|LIST~} is read from left to right, starting from the empty set: \code{\verb~|name~} or \code{\verb~|+name~} adds a switch, \code{\verb~|-name~} removes it, \code{\verb~|none~} empties the set, \code{\verb~|default~} adds \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~}, \code{\verb~|all~} adds the staging switches of ISA section 11 except \code{\verb~|k2~} (bits 0-10; no experiment bit old or new, not \code{\verb~|t2~}, \code{\verb~|lazyeval~}, \code{\verb~|levels-complete~}). Without the setting an engine runs \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~}. Examples: \code{\verb~|none~} = v0; \code{\verb~|default,probes~}; \code{\verb~|default,-same~}; \code{\verb~|default,k2~}. A switch that needs another one brings it, whatever the order of the list (\code{\verb~|Op.implied~}, applied to the final set and again by \code{\verb~|MachineEngine~}): \code{\verb~|skipargs~} brings \code{\verb~|facts~}, \code{\verb~|congruence~} brings \code{\verb~|probes~} - \code{\verb~|default,skipargs,-facts~} still runs \code{\verb~|facts~}. A strict engine (\code{\verb~|-X policy=strict~}, a strict \code{\verb~|EngineConfig~}) has no switch at all.}

\p{Related settings (not switches): \code{\verb~|-X machine.session-kib=N~} (the machine's own cap on a warm session, section "Sessions"), \code{\verb~|-X machine.unit-ticks=N~} (the machine's own tick bound per unit, default 2^27, NOTES-M6 F31), \code{\verb~|-X machine.hostDepth=N~} (host depth bound, default \code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} = 128), \code{\verb~|-X machine.eager-probe=N~} (with \code{\verb~|eager~}: the tick budget of one probe of the plain phase, default 2^22, 0 = none; finding INT7-F1 below the table of named switches), \code{\verb~|-X machine.cong-spend=N~} (with \code{\verb~|congruence~}: the ticks its segments may use in one declaration, default 2^18, 0 = no cap; below the table), \code{\verb~|-X machine.declines=FILE~} (one line per non-ACCEPT outcome of the machine), \code{\verb~|-X machine.debug=...~} (audits, README), \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.sizes=...~} (base table sizes, NOTES-INT I1), \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.keep=R,W,S~} and \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.pool=off~} (kept and pooled session arrays, NOTES-M6 F25).}
}

\subtree{
\title{The default configuration (integration of wave 6, 2026-11-24; the switch set of 2026-11-25)}

\table{
\tr{\th{What}\th{Default}\th{Decided by}}
\tr{\td{engine}\td{\strong{the machine} (\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} = 100 since 2026-11-25; it was 10 from 2026-11-24T20:35Z, and 100 from 19:41Z to 20:35Z). The reference engine re-checks every rejection and decides every unit the machine declines; \code{\verb~|-X engine=reference~} / \code{\verb~|-X policy=strict~} run the reference engine alone}\td{the gates of "The default set of 2026-11-25", S3's adversarial pass, the steward's gate on a machine-default distribution}}
\tr{\td{switch set \code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~}}\td{\strong{\code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,bodies,pchk,match,joint,code,casetrees,lazycases,directrules,lazyeval,same~}} (\code{\verb~|Op.SW_WAVE6~}, the set of 2026-11-24) \strong{+ \code{\verb~|eager,skipargs,congruence~}} (2026-11-25; \code{\verb~|skipargs~} brings \code{\verb~|facts~}, \code{\verb~|congruence~} brings \code{\verb~|probes~}; with the probe budget \code{\verb~|-X machine.eager-probe~} = 2^22 and the cap \code{\verb~|-X machine.cong-spend~} = 2^18): section "The default set of 2026-11-25"}\td{gates and measurements below, one line per switch in "Named switches"}}
\tr{\td{session cap \code{\verb~|MachineEngine.DEFAULT_SESSION_CAP~}}\td{\strong{1 MiB} (\code{\verb~|-X machine.session-kib=1024~})}\td{section "Sessions": 512 KiB and 1 MiB are equal within 2 \% everywhere, 2 and 4 MiB cost 3-4 \% CPU and wall clock on mathlib}}
\tr{\td{host depth bound \code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~}}\td{\strong{128}}\td{512 and 2048 measured: no gain (section "Host depth bound")}}
\tr{\td{Truffle tier (\code{\verb~|t2~}, module \code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~})}\td{\strong{off}; the jar is in every distribution and is used only under the switch}\td{T3's quiet numbers: parity on reachability, +38 \% wall at 8 workers on the Cedar slice, +39 \% on cedar (section "Truffle tier")}}
\tr{\td{universe levels}\td{the official relation (\code{\verb~|levels-complete~} off)}\td{owner note 11; both engines; the two arena imax corner cases are rejected}}
\tr{\td{platform}\td{CE native image \code{\verb~|-O3~} (the arena's binary); the JVM launcher is the faster platform once warm (table in \src{docs/BENCHMARKS.md})}\td{docs/PLATFORM.md, \code{\verb~|work/status/warm.md~}}}
}

\p{\strong{v0 is \code{\verb~|-X machine.switches=none~}.} The module's tests are not affected by the default set: \code{\verb~|pom.xml~} gives the test JVM \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.switches=none~}, and a \code{\verb~|Fixture~} engine has no switch unless the test names some. In force in EVERY configuration, v0 included, is the eager-reduction rule (section "Sessions": a declaration that enters eager reduction is declined) - a correctness rule, not an optimisation.}

\subtree{
\title{The default set of 2026-11-25 (INT7): wave 6 + \code{\verb~|eager~} + \code{\verb~|skipargs~} + \code{\verb~|congruence~}}

\p{Decided by warm wall clock on all eight corpora under the owner's notes 12 (warm wall clock, 8 workers, pipelined), 13 (the "practical" policy: kind T accepts are tolerated) and 16 (the fastest default), by the orchestrator's rule of 2026-11-25 00:17Z: primary = the geometric mean of the eight warm JVM pass times; guard = no corpus more than 3 \% slower than the set without the switch in question, over at least three interleaved rounds. JVM launcher, 8 workers, pipelined reload passes, every row in a \src{bench/quiet.py} window, the five sets interleaved round by round inside ONE window per corpus (rows \code{\verb~|work/int7/warm.tsv~}, table and the stages \code{\verb~|work/status/machine-int7.md~}). A cell = the mean over the rounds of the median later pass, s \verb~|[~rounds; min..max\verb~|]~; change against \code{\verb~|default,eager~} (here \code{\verb~|default~} is the set of wave 6). con-leche and reachability with the final settings (probe budget 2^22, cap 2^18).}

