\p{\code{\verb~|default,eager,skipargs,congruence~} has the lowest geometric mean (1.720 s; \code{\verb~|default,eager~} 1.980 s; the set of wave 6 2.065 s) and is at most 1.8 \% slower than \code{\verb~|default,eager~} on any corpus (reachability); \code{\verb~|eager~} is at most 2.2 \% slower than the set without it (con-leche, after the repair of INT7-F1 below). The one borderline cell: \code{\verb~|skipargs~} on top of \code{\verb~|congruence~} on reachability, +3.7 \% by the median of an eight-round window (12 ms on a pass measured in steps of 10 ms; +2.1 \% by the mean of its warm passes), against -17 \% on navier-stokes-euler and -4.7 \% on cslib. Adversarial pass with official verdicts for exactly this set: reviewer S3, no kind F (\src{docs/design/review/soundness-default-set.md} section 10); the shortcuts are theory-sound as implemented (S2, \code{\verb~|soundness-shortcuts.md~}). Gates of the set (frozen tree = this jar; reports \code{\verb~|work/status/machine-gate-int7-tF-default-tree.md~}, \code{\verb~|machine-mutants-tree.md~}): M8 full gate PASS WITH DECLINES (all 230 tests 15,804 accepted / 41 rejected / 0 declined; Init 57,938 / 0; Std 100,095 / 1 declined by the E1-F6 rule; reachability 4,224 / 0; Cedar slice 8,064 / 0; SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0); mutants 17,775 for v0 and for the set: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0; \code{\verb~|SHostileSlowTest~} 56 switch sets x 1,196 rows; DiffEngine through the launcher 1,141,195 checks (230 tests, Init, Std, cedar, cslib, 16 Mathlib slices), 0 differences; the eight corpora accepted with 8 and 4 workers.}
}

