\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|eager~}}\td{26 \code{\verb~|SW_EAGER~}}\td{E1 (M4, M5, M6, M3)}\td{a declaration that enters eager reduction (\code{\verb~|eagerReduce _ _~}) stays on the machine instead of being declined (M6-F26): the eager comparison is deferred to the end of the declaration and run under the official mode; the mode-dependent points of the plain phase are recorded and verified there (a difference declines); an eager-only event inside the K rule's comparison declines; such a declaration does not share a warm session (\src{docs/design/review/eager-reduction.md})}\td{\strong{ON by default} (2026-11-25, INT7; section "The default set of 2026-11-25")}\td{E1: declines Init 164 / Std 203 / cedar 423 / Mathlib 6,711 -> 0; differential \code{\verb~|default,eager~} clean on every corpus; 18 hostile rows declined by design (\code{\verb~|eager-hard~}); warm wall clock 8 workers JVM: Std -11 \% .. -22 \%, cedar -7 \% .. -10 \%}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|convexpect~}}\td{27 \code{\verb~|SW_CONV_EXPECT~}}\td{E1 (M5)}\td{B9 (\code{\verb~|expect~}) also when the lambda's domain is only convertible with the expected one, as before the fix of E1-F4 (off: only when they are one value); accepts the kind T rows \code{\verb~|e1-lam-fvar-type-in-conv-*~} (\src{docs/design/review/official-divergence.md})}\td{off}\td{E1: ticks -2.4 \% on the Cedar slice, -0.3 \% on Std; no gain in warm wall clock on cedar / Std (native, 8 workers)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|skipargs~}}\td{28 \code{\verb~|SW_SKIPARGS~}}\td{M4 (\code{\verb~|Conv.skipArgs~}, \code{\verb~|Cargs.plan~} / \code{\verb~|skipMask~}, \code{\verb~|Conv.k_etas3~}; masks in \code{\verb~|Facts~})}\td{CARGS and ETAS do not compare the positions the fact record of the head allows: proof positions under the agreement rule (B3), positions the definition does not read under SAMEDEF (B4), the Prop mask of structure eta. \strong{Brings \code{\verb~|facts~}} (\code{\verb~|Op.implied~}: it reads the fact records). The answer is derivable but not always the official verdict: KIND T (finding S-F2; OWNER-NOTES 13). Never in \code{\verb~|all~}; off in strict mode like every switch. Until 2026-11-25 the option \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.m4=skipargs~} (still read: the same shortcut without the implication)}\td{\strong{ON by default} (2026-11-25, INT7; section "The default set of 2026-11-25")}\td{theory-sound as implemented (S2, \src{docs/design/review/soundness-shortcuts.md}; optional patch H1 taken: \code{\verb~|Cargs.plan~} tests the level lists of the two heads itself); no kind F in \code{\verb~|default,eager~} + both shortcuts on 987 hostile rows (S3, \code{\verb~|soundness-default-set.md~} section 10); with \code{\verb~|congruence~}: Mathlib -24.6 \% native warm (25.4 -> 19.2 s), cslib -15 \%, navier-stokes-euler about -50 \% of the checks, con-leche +5.6 \% CPU (P9)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|congruence~}}\td{29 \code{\verb~|SW_CONGRUENCE~}}\td{M4 (\code{\verb~|Conv.congruence~}, \code{\verb~|convB1~}, \code{\verb~|convB12~}, \code{\verb~|convCore1~}; \code{\verb~|Same~}, \code{\verb~|Cong~})}\td{the same-head probe B1 (arguments of two applications of one head compared before either side is unfolded), closure congruence B12 (two closures of one term: slots by CONV) and proofs by type B2, as speculative segments under the probe budget and debt. \strong{Brings \code{\verb~|probes~}} (\code{\verb~|Op.implied~}). KIND T (finding S-F1). Never in \code{\verb~|all~}; off in strict mode. Until 2026-11-25 the option \code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.m4=congruence~}}\td{\strong{ON by default} (2026-11-25, INT7; section "The default set of 2026-11-25")}\td{as \code{\verb~|skipargs~}; the same-head probe costs on con-leche's hot unit (P9, P8)}}
}

\p{\strong{\code{\verb~|eager~}: the probes of the plain phase run under a budget (finding INT7-F1, 2026-11-25).} A declaration that may defer eager comparisons checks, in its plain phase, the two points where the official kernel answers differently under eager reduction - a Nat folding of an open pair and the test \code{\verb~|X = Bool.true~} on an open \code{\verb~|X~} - by running the eager branch as a probe (\code{\verb~|Conv.lazydProbe~}, \code{\verb~|Conv.convBoolProbe~}). The official plain procedure never starts that evaluation, and it can be of any size: with \code{\verb~|eager~} as published on 2026-11-24 the machine evaluated one unit of con-leche (\code{\verb~|ConLeche.lpOfData_pack~}) for 28.6 M ticks into the hard limit of a session (\code{\verb~|E_MEM~}, 3.3 GB), twice (cold retry), before the reference engine decided it in under a millisecond: 14.0 s instead of about 3 s for the warm pass of that corpus (JVM, 8 workers), and 8.6 to 11 GB resident on the native image. A probe is now a speculative segment with a budget of 2^22 ticks (\code{\verb~|-X machine.eager-probe~}; 2^23 until the measurement below); cut at it, the plain procedure goes on as the official one does, no further probe is started in the declaration, and the declaration is DECLINED if it has entered or enters eager reduction (\code{\verb~|machine.eager.declined.probe~}; the reference engine decides it; the cold retry is answered at once). Probes that complete on the eight corpora (\code{\verb~|machine.eager.probeMaxTicks~}): 63,654 ticks on Init / Std / cedar, 193 on con-leche, 102 on reachability, about 400 on navier-stokes-euler, 2,752,617 on cslib and mathlib (one unit of Mathlib, 4.14 M ticks in all; a budget of 2^21 declines it, 2^20 two more units). What the one cut probe costs con-leche (JVM, warm, 8 workers, three interleaved rounds): 1.287 s without \code{\verb~|eager~}; with it 1.403 s at 2^23 (+9.1 \%), 1.307 s at 2^22 (+1.6 \%), 1.283 s at 2^21 and 2^20 - hence 2^22. Regression tests: \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest.aProbeThatIsCutDeclinesTheUnitIfItEntersEagerReduction~}, \code{\verb~|SHostileEagerTest.aBudgetOfOneTickForTheProbesNeverChangesAVerdict~}.}

\p{\strong{\code{\verb~|congruence~}: a cap on what its segments use in one declaration (INT7, 2026-11-25).} The probe debt (NOTES-M4 D25) bounds what FAILING probes cost; a same-head probe (B1) or a closure congruence (B12) that answers T can still cost more than the unfolding it replaces, when the arguments are large closures that are walked slot by slot (P9 section 4.7). con-leche's \code{\verb~|ConLeche.Cached.reduceNatI._mutual.eq_def~}, the heaviest unit of that corpus, needs 3.84 M ticks without the switch and 7.21 M with it, and the corpus's warm pass was 4.3 \% slower with \code{\verb~|congruence~} and 8.5 \% with both shortcuts. \code{\verb~|Frames.k_try~} now reports what a segment used (\code{\verb~|Machine.tryUsed~}), \code{\verb~|Conv.Ext.spend~} sums it over the congruence segments of the declaration (a segment inside a segment counts twice), and at \code{\verb~|-X machine.cong-spend~} (default 2^18 ticks, 0 = no cap) \code{\verb~|Conv.congruence~} starts no further segment in that declaration: the unit needs 4.17 M ticks. What the cap costs where the switch wins, in ticks of the whole corpus with both shortcuts: navier-stokes-euler 144.4 M -> 149.5 M (548.2 M without the shortcuts), cslib 217.6 M -> 217.6 M (350.2 M), con-leche 80.1 M -> 76.7 M (84.4 M). Test: \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest.theCongruenceSegmentsOfADeclarationHaveATickCap~}.}

\p{The experiment bits that are still free or undecided: \code{\verb~|m1a~}, \code{\verb~|m1b~} (unused in published code), \code{\verb~|m2b~} (above), \code{\verb~|m3b~}, \code{\verb~|m4b~}, \code{\verb~|m7b~} (free). \code{\verb~|Op.SW_EXPERIMENTS~} names exactly these six; the six that entered the default set keep their old names as second names (\code{\verb~|m2a~} = \code{\verb~|bodies~}, ...).}

\subtree{
\title{\code{\verb~|same~}: why it is on although the soundness reviewer (package S) had ended before attacking it}

\p{\code{\verb~|Same.same(a, b)~} answers T only when it has SEEN the two values read back to the same expression, up to the normalisations the value model applies everywhere (beta and zeta of EVAL, canonical literals, PEEK); it calls no judgment and looks at no type, so it is not one of the congruence shortcuts of finding S-F1 (it never asks whether two DIFFERENT sub-terms are convertible). That is the condition under which value identity itself (\code{\verb~|a == b~} is T, in v0) gives the official verdict. Evidence beyond M4's (shortcheck on the four corpora: every T re-derived by the complete procedure; \code{\verb~|M4SameTest~}, \code{\verb~|M4OfficialTest~}): the hostile matrix above with \code{\verb~|same~} alone, on step 1 and in the default set (329 official verdicts each); the gate of the default set, whose audit lane re-derives every T of \code{\verb~|same~} under \code{\verb~|shortcheck~} on all 230 tests and the four corpora; 17,775 mutants; DiffEngine on the corpora. It has had no independent adversarial review: \code{\verb~|-X machine.switches=default,-same~} is the way back, at the cost above on Cedar and of the decline of \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~}.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{Sessions (the cap)}

\p{A warm session (\code{\verb~|warm~}) ends: on every outcome other than ACCEPT; when the next declaration is not later in file order; at the driver's cap (\code{\verb~|-X session-mib~}, default for the machine 4 MiB); and at \strong{the machine's own cap}, \code{\verb~|-X machine.session-kib=N~} (default \strong{1024} = 1 MiB, 0 = none; \code{\verb~|MachineEngine.DEFAULT_SESSION_CAP~}): before a declaration the machine forgets everything once \code{\verb~|Machine.engineBytes()~} exceeds it (statistic \code{\verb~|machine.capResets~}). The caps compose: the smaller one resets first.}

\p{Why so small: the instruction count FALLS as the cap grows (more memo hits) while CPU time and wall clock RISE (the tables leave the cache). M6's sweeps for \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} are in NOTES-M6 (F24); for the default set the rows "cap 512 KiB / 2 MiB / 4 MiB" of the table above: 512 KiB and 1 MiB are within 2 \% of each other on every corpus (one row each, so no ranking), 2 MiB costs 3-4 \% CPU on Init, Std, cedar and mathlib, 4 MiB 4-7 \% and 17 \% of wall clock on cedar. The orchestrator's question of 16:52Z (P8: +17 \% ticks on a Mathlib slice at 1 MiB against 4 MiB) is answered by wall clock on ALL of mathlib: 29.3 s per warm pass at 1 MiB against 30.6 / 30.3 s at 2 / 4 MiB (8 workers): the cap stays.}

\p{\strong{Eager reduction} (not a switch: a rule of the facade in EVERY configuration; NOTES-M6 F26). A declaration that enters eager reduction (an argument \code{\verb~|eagerReduce _ _~}) is DECLINED by the machine (\code{\verb~|E_LIMIT~}, \code{\verb~|UNSUPPORTED_INPUT~}, statistic \code{\verb~|machine.eagerDeclines~}; the reference engine decides it), and nothing it derived is kept. Reason: conversion under eager reduction depends on the mode and on the official kernel's per-declaration caches, which tables keyed by canonical values cannot reproduce (findings M6-F26, S-F4, S-F5). 164 of Init's declarations, 203 of Std's, 11 of the Cedar slice's, 8 of reachability's, 6,711 of mathlib's (0.94 \%; 11-12 \% of the workers' CPU there, P8). \code{\verb~|M6GuardTest~} fails if any class but \code{\verb~|Machine~} sets \code{\verb~|ER~} to a constant. Taking these declarations back is the first item of the list "what is left" in the integration log.}
}

\subtree{
\title{Host depth bound}

\p{\code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} = 128. Window \code{\verb~|w4~} (native, 8 workers, default set, warm pass wall / CPU): reachability 0.61, 0.58 s / 1.60, 1.55 s at 128, 0.60 / 1.64 at 512, 0.64 / 1.66 at 2048; Cedar slice 0.46 / 2.50 at 128, 0.50 / 2.53, 0.46 / 2.43; cedar 2.06, 2.11 / 14.01, 14.25 at 128, 2.18 / 14.47, 2.19 / 14.18. No corpus gains (M3 had found the same on reachability with one worker); the bound stays, and with it the worker stack the driver gives.}
}

\subtree{
\title{Truffle tier}

\p{\code{\verb~|rlvm-truffle~} (owner T3 since 16:31Z) is a reactor module and its jar is in every distribution; the tier runs only under \code{\verb~|t2~}. It is off: T2 found no gain; T3's quiet windows (NOTES-T3; warm wall clock per pass with one engine kept over the passes, K1 = \code{\verb~|default,code,casetrees~} of 16:24Z) give parity on reachability (JVM, 8 workers: 520 against 529 ms), +38 \% on the Cedar slice (232 -> 321 ms) and +39 \% on cedar (1,315 -> 1,827 ms; 1,820 blocks, 52.6 s of compilation that takes cores from the workers), +2 to +4 \% on the native image. The time of a block is in the interning probes it calls, not in the dispatch the tier removes.}
}

\subtree{
\title{Build flag measured, not adopted by the default build: the H10 inline lists}

\p{\src{rlvm-machine/h10/native-image-args.sh} (\code{\verb~|-H:PriorityForceInline~} of every continuation step, NeverInline of the slow paths), image \code{\verb~|work/int6/dist-a-h10~} against \code{\verb~|work/int6/dist-a~} (same jars), window \code{\verb~|w4~}, two interleaved rounds, CPU of the warm pass: Init 5.38, 5.37 -> 5.29, 5.32 (-1.3 \%); Std 10.23, 10.19 -> 10.22, 10.06 (-0.7 \%); Cedar slice 2.50, 2.51 -> 2.39, 2.40 (-4.4 \%); reachability 1.60, 1.55 -> 1.60, 1.59 (+1.3 \%, inside its spread); cedar 14.01, 14.25 -> 13.91, 13.97 (-1.3 \%); wall clock equal. A gain of 1-4 \% by the keep rule, except that reachability is not resolved. Not wired into \src{scripts/build.sh}: the lists are generated with \code{\verb~|javap~} and \code{\verb~|unzip~} at build time, and the arena build must first be shown to have both (\code{\verb~|scripts/build.sh ... --ni-arg ARG~} for every word the script prints builds such an image today).}
}

\subtree{
\title{Changing a default}

\ol{
\li{the owner sends the evidence (diff reports on all 230 + four corpora at the default cap, the measurement rows) in \code{\verb~|requests.log~};}
\li{the integrator re-runs M8's gate (\code{\verb~|report.sh gate --switches LIST~}) and the mutants on the published tree, asks for open soundness findings, and measures the candidate against the current default in ONE quiet window (\src{bench/warm.sh}, cedar and mathlib included);}
\li{\code{\verb~|Op.SW_DEFAULT~}, this file and \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest~} change together; \code{\verb~|-X machine.switches=none~} stays the way back to v0, and the strict engine is unaffected.}
}
}
